// Albert -- Win32 resources.
//
// Resource ID 1 is load-bearing twice over. The shell shows the lowest-
// numbered icon in an executable as the file's icon, and SDL3 does the same
// thing for the window class: with no SDL_HINT_WINDOWS_INTRESOURCE_ICON set it
// enumerates RT_GROUP_ICON and takes the first, "like in the Explorer"
// (SDL_windowsevents.c, WIN_RegisterApp). So this one entry covers Explorer,
// the taskbar and the title bar, and nothing in the C++ has to ask for it.
//
// albert.ico is generated, not hand-drawn -- see tools/make_icon.py, which
// lays the caricature out in a unit square and cuts every size from 16 to 256
// out of it. Re-run that script rather than editing the .ico.
1 ICON "albert.ico"
